<title>FRANCE: CYCLING-LEADING ETOILE DE BESSEGES RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-LEADING ETOILE DE BESSEGES RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LAUDIN, France 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings in</p>
<p>Saturday's fourth stage of the Etoile de Besseges cycle race</p>
<p>over 139 kms around Laudin.</p>
<p>1. Emmanuel Magnien (France) Festina  three hours 12 minutes 57</p>
<p>seconds</p>
<p>2. Zbigniew Spruch (Poland) Mapei</p>
<p>3. Jann Kirsipuu (Estonia) Casino</p>
<p>4. Gabriele Balducci (Italy) TRefin</p>
<p>5. Jo Planckaert (Belgium) Lotto</p>
<p>6. Andrei Tchmil (Ukraine) Lotto</p>
<p>7. Enrico Cassani (Italy) Polti</p>
<p>8. Steven de Jongh (Netherlands) TVM</p>
<p>9. Bruno Boscardin (Italy) Festina</p>
<p>10. Guido Wirz (Switzerland) Post Swiss  all same time as the</p>
<p>winner.</p>
<p>Overall:</p>
<p>1. Patrice Halgand (France) Festina 13 hours four minutes 35</p>
<p>seconds</p>
<p> 2. Spruch					   five seconds behind</p>
<p> 3 equal. Boscardin				    6 secs</p>
<p> 3 equal. Eros Poli (Italy) GAN		 same time</p>
<p> 5. Rodolfo Massi (Italy) Casino		  10</p>
<p> 6. Laurent Roux (France) TVM		     12</p>
<p> 7. Jan Svorada (Czech Republic) Mapei	1:39</p>
<p> 8. Ruben Galvan (Spain) Kelme		  1:51</p>
<p> 9. Magnien					   1:54</p>
<p> 10. De Jongh					 same time</p>
